# Architecture Documentation Maintenance

The folder `docs/architecture/` is the living, detailed architecture reference for the Studio. It contains one file per topic area, listed in `docs/architecture/index.md`. Each file documents internal implementation details: file paths, type definitions, method signatures, event flows, data models, and relationships between subsystems.

## When to update

Update the appropriate file in `docs/architecture/` whenever:

- You modify code that changes the architecture (new types, renamed methods, changed event wiring, new commands, new files, moved responsibilities)
- You gain significant new understanding of a Studio subsystem through research — even if you did not edit any code
- You discover that existing documentation is incorrect, incomplete, duplicated, or one-off history

For a lookup table mapping "what changed" to "which file to update", see the `architecture-docs` skill.

## What to write

- Concrete, technical content: file paths, type signatures, method tables, event flow diagrams, data model descriptions
- Keep it factual and reference-oriented — this is not a tutorial, it is a technical reference for agents
- Overview: 3–4 sentences. Point to other files; do not copy their tables
- The document is written in English. Maintain that language.

## Adding new topics

When documenting a subsystem that does not fit any existing file, create a new file in `docs/architecture/` and add it to the topic list in `docs/architecture/index.md`.

## Special-purpose files

- **`common-pitfalls.md`** — Recurring constraints someone could hit **again**. Gate: “Would a competent person hit this without this note?” If no, it does not belong here. Format: title = the constraint; Mistake / Why / Correct approach (3–8 lines); optional short snippet. No dates, no “Fixed (…)”, no named failing tests as headlines, no CI logs, no investigation novels. Test-harness facts go in `docs/testing.md`.
- **`docs/decisions.md`** (top-level, not in `architecture/`) — Significant A-vs-B choices that still explain the architecture. Format: Context / Options / Decision / short Rationale / `See architecture/….md`. Bugfixes, session diaries, upgrade play-by-plays, and Cursor-rule meta do not belong here. Superseded items are one-line stubs.

Plugin **how-to** lives in `docs/plugin-development-guide.md`. Host / sandbox / IPC: `plugin-host.md`. Manifest schema: `plugin-manifest.md`. iframe protocol: `webviews.md`. BPMN/DMN plugin APIs: the enrichment files. Do not reprint those tables in the guide.

## What NOT to do

- Do not delete still-accurate facts
- Do rewrite, merge, or drop content that is wrong, duplicated across files, or one-off history (incident reports, “what we tried”, Phase banners, dead roadmap links)
- Do not append a session strip to the bottom of a file
- Do not paste test postmortems into `common-pitfalls.md`
- Do not duplicate information already in `docs/systeme.md` or `docs/philosophie.md` (those cover high-level concepts; `docs/architecture/` covers implementation detail)
